    "body": "Reachability search (bounded grep on upstream/main 53a52f88: every place a `Move::axis` is set in `crates/{cl,motion,app,sim,post}/src`, the CL text reader, the project loader, `crates/app/src/mcp/`):\n\n- **Generators: no.** A move's axis is set through `Move::with_axis`, `ToolpathBuilder::set_axis` + `attach_axis` (the builder's own value), `TiltedFrame::new` or `angles_to_axis`. All four go through `cl::pose::normalize_axis`, which refuses a non-finite vector or one shorter than 1e-12 and normalises the rest. The raw `axis: Some(..)` literals outside tests are the sim's own stock replay (`field_rotary.rs`, `stock_sim_rotary.rs`), the tool-body wire view and verify's internal `c_steel` station pose. All of them are unit or rotated-unit. `motion/multiaxis/stamp_link.rs` copies an axis that is already normalised.\n- **CL text import: no.** `cl::text` rebuilds a pose from A/B/C through `angles_to_axis` (finite angles only, normalised).\n- **MCP: no.** No MCP tool takes raw moves or a raw axis. Poses enter through setup and frame angles, which go through `angles_to_axis` / `TiltedFrame::new`.\n- **Project loader: partly.** `MoveDto::to_move` attaches a cached path's stored axis VERBATIM (on purpose, for the save-load-save byte law). `project/validate.rs` refuses non-finite values (`all_finite`; JSON cannot carry inf/NaN anyway). A hand-edited project file can still hold a non-unit or zero axis such as `[0,0,7]` or `[0,0,0]`. That cached path is not re-verified on load (its stored warnings ride along), so this is the general \"tampered cache bypasses verify\" case, not an axis-specific hole. Regenerating the op re-verifies it, and the new door now normalises or refuses it there.\n- **Latent edge, informational:** `normalize_axis` squares its components unscaled. A finite vector with a component above ~1e154 makes `len` overflow to inf and returns `[0,0,0]` instead of refusing it. No caller passes such a vector. The verify door (PR below) now refuses a zero axis by name, so it cannot pass silently.\n\nResult: no generator, importer or MCP path is known to emit a non-finite or non-unit axis into verify, so this stays **P3** (not re-rated P1).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
